(6397367, 948282, 96614, '<td valign="top">Nicely done!  From a technical point of view, I would suggest a little fill light... the light from the back is done nicely (coming from both sides) but your face could use a little fill light... If you got a collapsible reflector and held it up camera left it should reflect some of the light coming from behind you onto your face... good luck!</td>', 'Nicely done!  From a technical point of view, I would suggest a little fill light... the light from the back is done nicely (coming from both sides) but your face could use a little fill light... If you got a collapsible reflector and held it up camera left it should reflect some of the light coming from behind you onto your face... good luck!', '2011-04-27 17:49:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6397369, 948128, 96614, '<td valign="top">Great idea!  I would like to see a little more of an expression on his face.  Also, it looks like the focus is on the broccoli rather than on his face... try stopping down your aperture to add more depth of field (so that his face will also be in focus...)</td>', 'Great idea!  I would like to see a little more of an expression on his face.  Also, it looks like the focus is on the broccoli rather than on his face... try stopping down your aperture to add more depth of field (so that his face will also be in focus...)', '2011-04-27 17:51:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6397370, 948235, 96614, '<td valign="top">Nice capture!</td>', 'Nice capture!', '2011-04-27 17:52:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6397372, 948299, 125975, '<td valign="top">Delightful!</td>', 'Delightful!', '2011-04-27 17:54:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6397373, 948217, 96614, '<td valign="top">Great idea!  Next time try to crop off the bottom because that out of focus ledge is a bit distracting.  I know it''s tricky, but try to get a shot with the lions head tilted up a bit so that there is more of a catch light in the eyes... I know that this ma require you to hang around the lion cage for a long time, but it will make all the difference when you can see the deep orange eyes lit up.</td>', 'Great idea!  Next time try to crop off the bottom because that out of focus ledge is a bit distracting.  I know it''s tricky, but try to get a shot with the lions head tilted up a bit so that there is more of a catch light in the eyes... I know that this ma require you to hang around the lion cage for a long time, but it will make all the difference when you can see the deep orange eyes lit up.', '2011-04-27 17:54:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6397375, 948284, 96614, '<td valign="top">Great capture!  I know you don''t want to hear it, and that it''s probably a little out of your control, but those branches in the bottom corners are a bit distracting.</td>', 'Great capture!  I know you don''t want to hear it, and that it''s probably a little out of your control, but those branches in the bottom corners are a bit distracting.', '2011-04-27 17:55:57.000000', NULL, 1),
