(6404204, 948118, 123348, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jomari:</b></div><hr/><i> This gave me a giggle and I gave you an 8. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thank you Marion and thanks to everyone for the wonderful comments and since it made most laugh I did succeed in what I set out to do :)!</td>', 'Originally posted by jomari: This gave me a giggle and I gave you an 8.  Thank you Marion and thanks to everyone for the wonderful comments and since it made most laugh I did succeed in what I set out to do :)!', '2011-05-04 14:15:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404226, 948047, 125275, '<td valign="top">I think the huge umbrellas behind you are perfect for this shot and a great idea. It''s almost like two big eyes waiting, watching...to see who might be coming...to take your lenses!<br/> <br/>But it also draws your attention down to the action in the shot. I wouldn''t have thought of putting umbrellas there, but it totally adds to the picture.</td>', 'I think the huge umbrellas behind you are perfect for this shot and a great idea. It''s almost like two big eyes waiting, watching...to see who might be coming...to take your lenses! But it also draws your attention down to the action in the shot. I wouldn''t have thought of putting umbrellas there, but it totally adds to the picture.', '2011-05-04 14:44:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404233, 948118, 129195, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 9. Funny, revealing, suggestive but not crude. I thought it was very well done :)</td>', 'I gave this a 9. Funny, revealing, suggestive but not crude. I thought it was very well done :)', '2011-05-04 14:53:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404252, 948047, 123601, '<td valign="top">sharing is carrring</td>', 'sharing is carrring', '2011-05-04 15:03:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404319, 948118, 91783, '<td valign="top">i think because it is suggestive that that is why many people voted it lower. I gave you a 5 and here are the reasons why.<br/> <br/>I think it could be sharper. And with the choice of bw, your subject almost blends into the bg. atleast to me it does. maybe you could add some contrast and brighten him up a little? I do think its a funny image and its not really showing anything. just a balloon or two. lol creativity wise i think that its a good image.</td>', 'i think because it is suggestive that that is why many people voted it lower. I gave you a 5 and here are the reasons why. I think it could be sharper. And with the choice of bw, your subject almost blends into the bg. atleast to me it does. maybe you could add some contrast and brighten him up a little? I do think its a funny image and its not really showing anything. just a balloon or two. lol creativity wise i think that its a good image.', '2011-05-04 16:38:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404370, 948263, 40391, '<td valign="top">Well, I liked this and gave it a 6 - thanks for the laugh.</td>', 'Well, I liked this and gave it a 6 - thanks for the laugh.', '2011-05-04 17:53:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404389, 948047, 59029, '<td valign="top">What, no Nikon 300mm f/4?! *shakes head in disbelief*  Good work Eric, and good to see you back on here too!  Congrats on the blue!</td>', 'What, no Nikon 300mm f/4?! *shakes head in disbelief*  Good work Eric, and good to see you back on here too!  Congrats on the blue!', '2011-05-04 18:21:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404390, 948047, 96614, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by adigitalromance:</b></div><hr/><i> I think the huge umbrellas behind you are perfect for this shot and a great idea. It''s almost like two big eyes waiting, watching...to see who might be coming...to take your lenses!<br/> <br/>But it also draws your attention down to the action in the shot. I wouldn''t have thought of putting umbrellas there, but it totally adds to the picture. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>yea, I purposely aimed them inwards to give kind of animate them with the same expression as my face... as thought they were looking over my shoulders... I had always wanted to incorporate the umbrellas into a picture and I wasn''t sure if they would cause any lens flare, and apparently they don''t  =)<br/> <br/>thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by adigitalromance: I think the huge umbrellas behind you are perfect for this shot and a great idea. It''s almost like two big eyes waiting, watching...to see who might be coming...to take your lenses! But it also draws your attention down to the action in the shot. I wouldn''t have thought of putting umbrellas there, but it totally adds to the picture.   yea, I purposely aimed them inwards to give kind of animate them with the same expression as my face... as thought they were looking over my shoulders... I had always wanted to incorporate the umbrellas into a picture and I wasn''t sure if they would cause any lens flare, and apparently they don''t  =) thanks!', '2011-05-04 18:21:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404391, 948047, 96614, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by wolf:</b></div><hr/><i> Love it Eric!!! Nice to see you''re back!!  Congrats on the blue! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!<br/> <br/>I''m going to try and enter at least one pic every other week to stay in the game... I started a new job and it took me a while to get settled... now I have the time to focus on challenges again...<br/> <br/>I hope to be in the running regularly again... probably not on the front page too often, but I''ll do my best  =)</td>', 'Originally posted by wolf: Love it Eric!!! Nice to see you''re back!!  Congrats on the blue!   Thanks! I''m going to try and enter at least one pic every other week to stay in the game... I started a new job and it took me a while to get settled... now I have the time to focus on challenges again... I hope to be in the running regularly again... probably not on the front page too often, but I''ll do my best  =)', '2011-05-04 18:23:48.000000', NULL, 0),
