(6405865, 948047, 132010, '<td valign="top">I have to be honest here. I rated this picture low because when I first saw it I disliked it immediately. The subject looked so greedy I was turned off the whole picture. When I saw that it had won, I looked at it with new eyes and started to appreciate the technical expertise required to shoot the photo and began to realize the power of the photo. It conveys it''s subject extremely well, so well that I still don''t like the photo! If I can ever take a photo that is half as powerful as this I will be happy.<br/>Great job Shutter-For-Hire.</td>', 'I have to be honest here. I rated this picture low because when I first saw it I disliked it immediately. The subject looked so greedy I was turned off the whole picture. When I saw that it had won, I looked at it with new eyes and started to appreciate the technical expertise required to shoot the photo and began to realize the power of the photo. It conveys it''s subject extremely well, so well that I still don''t like the photo! If I can ever take a photo that is half as powerful as this I will be happy.Great job Shutter-For-Hire.', '2011-05-06 17:57:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6406118, 948047, 96614, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by heatherd:</b></div><hr/><i> Let me know if ever you think of selling any lens. :-)Now, tell us which is your favourite lens??? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hmmm... favorite???  well, It''s a really tough call... I really do like to shoot wide so I''d lean towards the Tokina 12-24 used for the shoot, but all the lenses serve their purpose...  I use the 35mm f/2D for all portrait sessions, the macro lenses for.. well macro shots,... ect...<br/> <br/>They do all get used on occasion...  =)</td>', 'Originally posted by heatherd: Let me know if ever you think of selling any lens. :-)Now, tell us which is your favourite lens???   hmmm... favorite???  well, It''s a really tough call... I really do like to shoot wide so I''d lean towards the Tokina 12-24 used for the shoot, but all the lenses serve their purpose...  I use the 35mm f/2D for all portrait sessions, the macro lenses for.. well macro shots,... ect... They do all get used on occasion...  =)', '2011-05-06 22:12:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6406121, 948047, 96614, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Eaglerapids:</b></div><hr/><i> I have to be honest here. I rated this picture low because when I first saw it I disliked it immediately. The subject looked so greedy I was turned off the whole picture. When I saw that it had won, I looked at it with new eyes and started to appreciate the technical expertise required to shoot the photo and began to realize the power of the photo. It conveys it''s subject extremely well, so well that I still don''t like the photo! If I can ever take a photo that is half as powerful as this I will be happy.<br/>Great job Shutter-For-Hire. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!  I just checked out your waterfall pics... they are amazing!  That''s going to be my summer project... mastering the waterfall...  look for me on the front page again  =P<br/> <br/>.</td>', 'Originally posted by Eaglerapids: I have to be honest here. I rated this picture low because when I first saw it I disliked it immediately. The subject looked so greedy I was turned off the whole picture. When I saw that it had won, I looked at it with new eyes and started to appreciate the technical expertise required to shoot the photo and began to realize the power of the photo. It conveys it''s subject extremely well, so well that I still don''t like the photo! If I can ever take a photo that is half as powerful as this I will be happy.Great job Shutter-For-Hire.   Thanks!  I just checked out your waterfall pics... they are amazing!  That''s going to be my summer project... mastering the waterfall...  look for me on the front page again  =P .', '2011-05-06 22:14:49.000000', NULL, 0),
